THE GRANT, AND ITS LIMIT
    By publishing this repository publicly on GitHub, the copyright holder has
    granted the licence required by GitHub's Terms of Service, section 5,
    License Grant to Other Users:

        "If you set your pages and repositories to be viewed publicly, you
        grant each User of GitHub a nonexclusive, worldwide license to use,
        display, and perform Your Content through the GitHub Service and to
        reproduce Your Content solely on GitHub as permitted through GitHub's
        functionality (for example, through forking)."

    THAT GRANT STANDS AND THIS FILE DOES NOT PURPORT TO OVERRIDE IT. Any GitHub
    user may view this repository and may fork it on GitHub.

    NO OTHER RIGHT IS GRANTED. Outside that grant, and outside GitHub's own
    functionality, no person is licensed to copy, modify, distribute, publish,
    sublicense, host, or create derivative works from the contents of this
    repository. GitHub's own documentation states the default position plainly:

        "without a license, the default copyright laws apply, meaning that you
        retain all rights to your source code and no one may reproduce,
        distribute, or create derivative works from your work."

    A licence file is included anyway, because "no licence" is ambiguous to a
    reader and this repository fronts a commercial product.

TRADEMARK
    ENVOLOK is a trademark of Range Art & Design LLC. Nothing in the GitHub
    grant above licenses the mark. Forking the repository does not license the
    name, and republishing this page under the ENVOLOK name is not permitted.

A NOTE ON WHAT THIS FILE CANNOT DO
    The scope of GitHub's fork right is not settled. GitHub's terms permit
    reproduction "solely on GitHub as permitted through GitHub's functionality",
    and reasonable readers disagree about whether that includes modifying a
    fork. This file does not resolve that question and does not pretend to.
    It states what is reserved and leaves the platform grant intact.

